C c-visitor-thorp-52 serverPARA="The Household Council governs Radhawadi. Its seat is held by Mahesh Bhat, the boat-headman and Household Elder. Radhawadi approves of the Household Council. It has lasted for centuries, and its people count that in favour of the Household Council."
C c-visitor-thorp-52 twinPARA="The Household Council governs Radhawadi. Its seat is held by Mahesh Bhat, the boat-headman and Household Elder. Radhawadi approves of the Household Council. It has lasted for centuries, and its people count that in favour of the Household Council."
C c-visitor-thorp-52 ownPARA="Mahesh Bhat, the boat-headman and Household Elder, holds the seat of the Household Council. The Household Council governs Radhawadi. Prosperity has earned the Household Council the approval of Radhawadi. Radhawadi has lasted for centuries, and its people count that in favour of the Household Council. Farms nearby have been abandoned after attacks. The community cannot agree on whether to shelter in place, build defences, or leave."
C c-visitor-hamlet-139 server bd={"food":0,"merits":10} score=55 legacy=null merits=["lasting"] | twin(default veil) bd={"food":0,"merits":10} merits=["lasting"] | own merits=["lasting"]
C c-visitor-hamlet-139 serverPARA="Kabahchihua is governed by the Elder Council. Quetzalli Chel, the mine captain and Elder, holds its seat. Kabahchihua tolerates the Elder Council, and no more. It has endured for generations, and its people give the Elder Council some of the credit."
C c-visitor-hamlet-139 twinPARA="Kabahchihua is governed by the Elder Council. Quetzalli Chel, the mine captain and Elder, holds its seat. Kabahchihua tolerates the Elder Council, and no more. It has endured for generations, and its people give the Elder Council some of the credit."
C c-visitor-hamlet-139 ownPARA="The Elder Council governs Kabahchihua. Its seat is held by Quetzalli Chel, the mine captain and Elder. Kabahchihua tolerates the Elder Council and no more. Crime is the reason. Kabahchihua has endured for generations, and its people give the Elder Council some of the credit. A dispute over field rotation and grazing rights has divided the village for most of this season."
